# EmailJS credentials for the /schedule meeting-request form.
#
# Copy this file to `.env` for local development. `.env` is gitignored.
#
# WINDOWS GOTCHA: do not create `.env` with PowerShell's
# `Set-Content -Encoding utf8` — Windows PowerShell 5.1 writes a UTF-8 BOM,
# and the BOM becomes part of the FIRST variable's name, so that one variable
# silently reads as undefined. Use `copy .env.example .env` and edit it, or
# write it with `[System.IO.File]::WriteAllText(path, text)`.
# For the deployed site these must ALSO exist as GitHub repo secrets
# (Settings -> Secrets and variables -> Actions), because Vite inlines them
# at build time inside the Actions runner — see .github/workflows/deploy.yml.
#
# Get them from https://dashboard.emailjs.com :
#   SERVICE_ID   Email Services -> your Gmail service
#   TEMPLATE_ID  Email Templates -> the meeting-request template
#   PUBLIC_KEY   Account -> General -> Public Key
#
# The public key is designed to be exposed in client code. It is not a secret.
# Do NOT put your EmailJS *private* key here — it would ship in the bundle.
#
# The template must use these variable names, matching the form field `name`
# attributes in src/pages/Schedule.jsx:
#   {{from_name}}  {{org}}  {{reply_to}}  {{meeting_datetime}}  {{details}}
# Set the template's "To" address to xanderminch@gmail.com.

VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_TEMPLATE_ID=
VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=
